Run 6 (`path odd`): a foreign URL: exit 2, no fetch (R-PTH3). Run 7 (`path pf` in p5): an alias that is not in the header: exit 2, the message lists the entries (R-PTH3); the project p5 is recorded all the same (R-PTH4: a run that found a project records it, also when it fails later). Run 8 (`path`, no alias): exit 2 before any call except `args` (R-PTH1, R-EC2). Run 9 (`path pf` at the root of a workspace with 2 members and no current member, answer Q1): exit 2 that lists the members, as `add` and `remove` do (R-WS12, R-PD5); nothing is fetched.

